Dependencies (not included)
---------------------------

The following are used but not distributed with this repository; each is
under its own license. The CMake build downloads nothing: it locates libzmq
and zmq.hpp, which must already be installed for a local build (it stops with
an install hint when either is missing), and uses OpenMP when the compiler
provides it. The Docker files and the CI workflow install the dependencies
(apt, pip, and the checksum-pinned cppzmq header); the Python packages for
the host-side demo and the tools are installed by the user:

- ZeroMQ: libzmq and the C++ header zmq.hpp (cppzmq), used by the servers
  and the coordinator;
- the C++ standard library and, when the compiler provides it, OpenMP
  (tide-build-pq);
- Python packages for the tools and tests: numpy, scipy, pymetis (METIS
  graph partitioning), diskannpy (Vamana graph construction) and pyzmq.
